# Copy to .lkmabt.env and fill locally. Never commit the copy.
# Provider commands read .lkmabt.env from the working directory automatically
# when it exists; a missing default file is fine. Pass --env-file <path> only to
# use a different file. cleanup reads no env file.
# Cluster selection lives in .lkmabt-clusters.yaml; this file holds provider credentials only.
# GITHUB_TOKEN and GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN are optional. Leave either empty to
# authenticate at run time: GitHub opens the gh browser flow; GitLab opens the
# personal access token page and prompts for the token. Use api and
# write_repository scopes; PaC rejects OAuth tokens. Only gh must be on PATH. LKMABT deletes the
# temporary tokens, and the temporary GitLab PaC Secret, when the run ends. A
# configured token needs api access to its fixture repository. A configured
# GITHUB_TOKEN is validated for App-installation listing, fixture push access,
# and repository listing for selected App installations; classic/OAuth tokens
# may need the read:user scope (gh auth refresh -h github.com -s read:user). In a
# terminal, a token that fails those checks falls back to the gh login.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
GITLAB_BOT_TOKEN=
GITLAB_API_URL=https://gitlab.com/api/v4
